-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Herpes simplex virus type 2 infection does not influence viral dynamics during early HIV-1 infection.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>195</volume><fpage>1270</fpage><lpage>1277</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17396995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001080-Cunningham1"><label>5</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cunningham</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dwyer</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The pathogenesis underlying the interaction of HIV and herpes simplex virus after co-infection.</article-title><source>J HIV Ther</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15071424</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001080-Bosnjak1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bosnjak</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Miranda-Saksena</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Koelle</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Boadle</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Herpes simplex virus infection of human dendritic cells induces apoptosis and allows cross-presentation via uninfected dendritic cells.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>174</volume><fpage>2220</fpage><lpage>2227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15699155</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001080-Jones1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Herc</surnam